<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="ko">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>수요 기반 MRP(DDMRP) 인터랙티브 대시보드</title>
    <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js"></script>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Noto+Sans+KR:wght@400;500;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <!-- Chosen Palette: Calm Neutrals -->
    <!-- Application Structure Plan: A single-page, thematic dashboard structure guides the user through a narrative: 1. The Problem (visualizing the Bullwhip Effect), 2. The Paradigm Shift (comparing MRP vs. DDMRP), 3. How It Works (interactive buffer simulation), and 4. The Impact (quantitative results). This structure was chosen to transform the static report into an engaging, educational experience. A sticky navigation bar allows for easy exploration, making complex SCM concepts tangible and memorable for a competition setting. -->
    <!-- Visualization & Content Choices: 
        - Bullwhip Effect (Problem): Report Info -> Goal: Demonstrate forecast amplification -> Viz: Interactive Line Chart (Chart.js) -> Interaction: User slides customer demand to see exaggerated upstream orders -> Justification: More impactful than a static image.
        - MRP vs DDMRP (Solution): Report Info -> Goal: Explain the core concept shift -> Viz: HTML/Tailwind diagram -> Interaction: User clicks on BOM nodes to place a "buffer," visually showing how it absorbs shock -> Justification: Makes the "decoupling" concept intuitive.
        - Buffer Simulation (How it Works): Report Info -> Goal: Demystify DDMRP mechanics -> Viz: Interactive HTML/CSS buffer funnel + data table -> Interaction: User inputs inventory/demand numbers to see the Net Flow level and priority change in real-time -> Justification: Hands-on simulation is the best way to teach the core logic.
        - Expected Benefits (Impact): Report Info -> Goal: Prove the business value -> Viz: Bar Charts (Chart.js) comparing Before/After DDMRP KPIs -> Interaction: Hover for details -> Justification: Clear, quantitative summary of the solution's value.
    -->
    <!-- CONFIRMATION: NO SVG graphics used. NO Mermaid JS used. -->
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif;
            background-color: #F8F9FA;
            color: #343A40;
        }
        .chart-container {
            position: relative;
            width: 100%;
            max-width: 800px;
            margin-left: auto;
            margin-right: auto;
            height: 300px;
            max-height: 400px;
        }
        @media (min-width: 768px) {
            .chart-container {
                height: 400px;
            }
        }
        .nav-link {
            transition: all 0.3s;
        }
        .nav-link.active {
            color: #1D4ED8;
            border-bottom-color: #1D4ED8;
        }
        .buffer-zone {
            transition: all 0.3s ease-in-out;
        }
        .net-flow-indicator {
            transition: bottom 0.5s ease-in-out;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body class="antialiased">
    <header class="bg-white/80 backdrop-blur-md shadow-sm sticky top-0 z-50">
        <nav class="container mx-auto px-6 py-3">
            <div class="flex justify-between items-center">
                <h1 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-800">SCM 혁신: DDMRP 도입 방안</h1>
                <div class="hidden md:flex space-x-8">
                    <a href="#problem" class="nav-link text-gray-600 hover:text-blue-600 border-b-2 border-transparent pb-1">문제 인식</a>
                    <a href="#solution" class="nav-link text-gray-600 hover:text-blue-600 border-b-2 border-transparent pb-1">해결 방안</a>
                    <a href="#simulation" class="nav-link text-gray-600 hover:text-blue-600 border-b-2 border-transparent pb-1">작동 원리</a>
                    <a href="#impact" class="nav-link text-gray-600 hover:text-blue-600 border-b-2 border-transparent pb-1">기대 효과</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </nav>
    </header>

    <main class="container mx-auto px-6 py-12">
        
        <!-- Section 1: Problem -->
        <section id="problem" class="mb-24 scroll-mt-20">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-center mb-4 text-gray-800">무엇이 문제일까요?</h2>
            <p class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center text-gray-600 mb-12">
                전통적인 자재소요량계획(MRP)은 '수요 예측'에 기반합니다. 하지만 예측이 조금만 빗나가도 공급망 전체가 흔들리는 '채찍 효과(Bullwhip Effect)'가 발생하여 막대한 재고 비용과 결품 손실을 유발합니다. 아래 시뮬레이터로 직접 확인해보세요.
            </p>
            <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-xl shadow-lg">
                <div class="chart-container">
                    <canvas id="bullwhipChart"></canvas>
                </div>
                <div class="mt-8 text-center">
                    <label for="demandSlider" class="block font-medium text-gray-700 mb-2">최종 고객 수요 변동률 조정</label>
                    <div class="flex items-center justify-center space-x-4">
                        <span class="text-sm text-gray-500">-10%</span>
                        <input id="demandSlider" type="range" min="-10" max="10" value="0" class="w-64">
